lesson: 170
title: The dog that runs back and forth
level: primary-4
stars: 3
explain: Do not follow each trip of the dog: only ask how long it runs. It runs for exactly as long as the two people walk until they meet.
explain: Two people 1200 m apart walk towards each other at 50 and 70 m a minute: they meet after 1200 / (50 + 70) = 10 minutes.
explain: A dog that runs between them at 200 m a minute all that time runs 200 × 10 = 2000 m, however many times it turns.
vars: a=name b=name u=40..80 v=40..80 w=150..250 t=5..15 z=2..9
need: (u + v) * t <= 2000
answer: w * t
exercise: {a} and {b} start at the same time {(u+v)*t} metres apart and walk towards each other, {a} at {u} metres a minute and {b} at {v} metres a minute. {a}'s dog starts with {a.him} and runs to {b} at {w} metres a minute, then back to {a}, and so on until the two meet. How many metres does the dog run?
exercise: Two friends walk towards each other from {(u+v)*t} metres apart, at {u} and {v} metres a minute. A puppy runs between them at {w} metres a minute without stopping until the friends meet. How far does the puppy run, in metres?
exercise: Two children on a {(u+v)*t}-metre path walk towards each other at {u} and {v} metres a minute. A dog runs from one to the other and back again at {w} metres a minute until the children meet. What distance does the dog cover?
exercise: {a} walks at {u} metres a minute and {b} at {v} metres a minute, towards each other, starting {(u+v)*t} metres apart. Their dog keeps running between them at {w} metres a minute. How many metres has it run when {a} and {b} meet?
exercise: Two hikers {(u+v)*t} m apart set off towards each other at {u} m and {v} m a minute. A dog, {w} m a minute, dashes from one hiker to the other again and again until they meet. How far does the dog run in all?
test: A dog runs {w} metres a minute. It runs to and fro between {a} and {b}, who walk towards each other at {v} and {u} metres a minute from {(u+v)*t} metres apart. How many metres has the dog run by the time they meet?
test: Two scouts are {(u+v)*t} metres apart and march towards each other, one at {u} metres a minute and one at {v}. Between them their {z}-year-old dog keeps running at {w} metres a minute, turning each time it reaches a scout. What total distance does it run before the scouts meet?
test: How far does a dog run if it races at {w} m a minute between two walkers until they meet, the walkers starting {(u+v)*t} m apart and walking towards each other at {u} m and {v} m a minute?
exercise: {a} and {b} are {(u+v)*t} metres apart in a park in Boston. They walk towards each other at {u} and {v} metres a minute, and {a}'s dog runs back and forth between them at {w} metres a minute until they meet. How far does the dog run, in metres?
exercise: How many metres does a dog run if it races to and fro at {w} metres a minute between two friends who start {(u+v)*t} metres apart and walk towards each other at {u} and {v} metres a minute, stopping when they meet?
exercise: Two walkers on a beach in Cornwall start {(u+v)*t} m apart and head towards each other at {v} m and {u} m per minute. Their sheepdog runs between them at {w} m per minute, turning round each time it reaches one of them, until they meet. What distance does the sheepdog cover?
exercise: A terrier runs at {w} metres a minute. It keeps running from {a} to {b} and back while they walk towards each other at {u} and {v} metres a minute from {(u+v)*t} metres apart. How many metres has it run when they meet?
exercise: Two cousins in Canada are {(u+v)*t} metres apart on a straight trail. They walk towards each other, one at {u} metres a minute and the other at {v}. A puppy dashes between them at {w} metres a minute the whole time. How far has the puppy run when the cousins meet?
exercise: {a} walks {u} metres per minute and {b} walks {v} metres per minute, towards each other, from {(u+v)*t} metres apart. A dog runs between them non-stop at {w} metres per minute until they meet. Find the total distance the dog runs.
exercise: Starting {(u+v)*t} metres apart in a field in Ireland, two farmers walk towards each other at {u} and {v} metres a minute. Their collie runs from one to the other and back again at {w} metres a minute. How many metres does the collie run before the farmers meet?
exercise: A dog runs between two friends at {w} m a minute while they close a gap of {(u+v)*t} m, walking towards each other at {u} m and {v} m a minute. How far does it run before they meet?
test: Two joggers in Melbourne start {(u+v)*t} metres apart and jog towards each other at {u} and {v} metres a minute. A seagull flies back and forth between them at {w} metres a minute until they meet. How many metres does the seagull fly?
test: {b}'s spaniel can run {w} metres in a minute. {a} and {b} set off towards each other from {(u+v)*t} metres apart, at {v} and {u} metres a minute, and the spaniel runs between them without stopping until they meet. What is the length of all its runs together?
test: What total distance does a dog cover running at {w} metres a minute between two people who walk towards each other at {u} and {v} metres a minute from {(u+v)*t} metres apart, if it stops when they meet?
test: Two rangers in a forest in Oregon walk towards each other at {u} and {v} metres a minute from {(u+v)*t} metres apart. One ranger's dog, {z} years old, runs back and forth between them at {w} metres a minute until they meet. How far does the dog run?
test: Between two hikers who are {(u+v)*t} m apart and walk towards each other at {u} m and {v} m a minute, a dog runs back and forth at {w} m a minute. When the hikers meet, how many metres has the dog run in total?
test: In a park in London, {a} and {b} walk towards each other from opposite gates {(u+v)*t} metres apart, at {u} and {v} metres a minute. {a}'s dog runs to {b}, back to {a}, and so on, at {w} metres a minute, until the two meet. How far does the dog run?
exercise: {a} n {b} {(u+v)*t} m apart, walk at each other {u} and {v} m a min, dog runs between at {w} m a min til they meet. how far dog run
exercise: puppy runs back n forth at {w+10} — no wait, {w} m a min, between 2 friends {(u+v)*t} m apart walking at {u} and {v}. how many metres puppy runs
exercise: Sam says dog runs {w} m cos that's its speed. nah wrong innit. friends {(u+v)*t} m apart walk at each other {u} n {v} m a min, dog {w} m a min til they meet. metres really?
exercise: 2 walkers {(u+v)*t} m apart, {u} and {v} m a min towards each other, dog's called Rex, he's {z} years old, runs {w} m a min between em til they meet. how far Rex go
test: 2 kids {(u+v)*t} m apart walking to each other at {u} n {v} m a min, dog zooms {w} m a min back n forth til they meet. metres the dog does?
test: {a} n {b} walk at {u} and {v} m/min, start {(u+v)*t+50} m apart — sorry, {(u+v)*t} m, towards each other. dog runs between at {w} m/min til they meet. how far dog go
test: dog runs {w} m a min between {a} and {b} until they meet, they start {(u+v)*t} m apart going {u} and {v} m a min at each other, {b}'s got a {z} kg bag lol. dog's distance?
exercise: {a}'s old dog Rex is no longer with us, so {a} brings the new puppy. {a} and {b} start {(u+v)*t} metres apart and walk towards each other, {a} at {u} and {b} at {v} metres a minute. The puppy runs between them at {w} metres a minute until they meet. How many metres does it run?
exercise: me and {b} walking at each other from {(u+v)*t} m, me at {u} m a minute, {b} at {v}. the dog — mum calls him "spirited", means bonkers — runs between us at {w} m a minute till we meet. how far's the stupid mutt run
test: The late Mr Brown's sheepdog now lives with {a}. When {a} and {b} walk towards each other from {(u+v)*t} metres apart ({a} at {u}, {b} at {v} metres a minute), the dog dashes back and forth between them at {w} metres a minute until they meet. Find the dog's distance in metres.
exam: It is given that {a} and {b} set out simultaneously from points {(u+v)*t} metres apart and walk towards each other at {u} and {v} metres per minute respectively, whilst a dog runs continuously between them at {w} metres per minute until they meet. Determine the total distance, in metres, covered by the dog.
exam: Whereas two friends advance towards each other from a separation of {(u+v)*t} metres, at speeds of {u} and {v} metres per minute respectively, and a puppy runs to and fro between them without interruption at {w} metres per minute, ascertain the distance in metres travelled by the puppy until the friends meet.
exam: Ascertain the distance in metres flown by a bird which flies back and forth at {w} metres per minute between two pedestrians, from the moment at which they, being {(u+v)*t} metres apart, begin to walk towards each other at {u} and {v} metres per minute until the moment of their meeting.
exam: {a} walks at {u} metres per minute towards {b}, who simultaneously walks towards {a.him} at {v} metres per minute, the initial separation being {(u+v)*t} metres. The dog of {a} runs at {w} metres per minute from one to the other incessantly until the two meet. State the total distance run by the dog, in metres.
